Found and fixed the real root cause. All three "hangs" today (Akira.1988, Alien.3.assembly.cut, Alien.Covenant.2017) turned out to be the same bug, and it wasn't about networking or S3 at all: the upload had already completed successfully every time (metadata.json already showed synced) — the script just never exited afterward, because main() only called process.exit() on the failure path. On success it fell through with nothing forcing termination, so the redis client's open socket kept Node's event loop alive forever. Since the parent script drives this via execFileSync (which blocks until the child fully exits, not just until its logical work is done), that hung the entire sequential backfill on literally every item.

Fixed by adding an explicit process.exit(0) after main() resolves in all three scripts, deployed, and restarted the backfill — it's now past the item that hung before and progressing. Monitor is re-armed and watching for further stalls or completion.

